.TH TRAILMATE-LINUX-AUDIO-PROBE 1 "October 2026" "Trail Mate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trailmate\-linux\-audio\-probe \- inspect Linux audio devices and PCM transport
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trailmate\-linux\-audio\-probe
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists SDL audio devices or performs a bounded mono PCM capture, reporting sample
counts, peak amplitude, dropped samples and capture shutdown state.
Captured samples are used to calculate statistics and then discarded.
An optional playback check queues 100 milliseconds of digital silence and waits
for the output transport to drain.
Acoustic microphone and speaker checks require separate observation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list\-devices
List the current audio driver and available capture and playback devices.
Without a capture duration, exit after listing devices.
.TP
.BI \-\-capture\-ms " N"
Capture for 100 to 5000 milliseconds. A duration is required unless devices are
only being listed.
.TP
.BI \-\-rate " N"
Set the requested sample rate from 8000 to 48000 Hz. The default is 15000 Hz.
.TP
.BI \-\-input " NAME"
Select a capture device by its SDL device name. By default, use the audio
system's default capture device.
.TP
.B \-\-play\-silence
After capture, check silent playback and output shutdown at the requested rate.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
trailmate-linux-audio-probe --list-devices
trailmate-linux-audio-probe --capture-ms 500 --rate 15000 --play-silence
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested device listing or capture/playback transport checks succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
An audio driver, capture, playback or shutdown check failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or values outside the supported ranges.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR trailmate-linux (1)
